    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "An oval cotton placemat is a 30 × 40 cm mat worked in double crochet outward from a foundation chain using "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "oval construction",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "oval-construction"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ". Stitches are worked along both sides of the starting chain, then increased at each short curved end to keep the oval flat. A beginner technique. The shaping is methodical and the increases are easy to count. One 100 m ball of DK cotton makes two mats."
          }
        ]
      },
